<protocol name="view_image" type="tool_mastery" domain="creative">

## PURPOSE

Master view_image - multimodal image viewing for visual analysis.
This tool gives you EYES. You SEE images directly, not descriptions.

---

## WHEN TO USE

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Source image provided | view_image IMMEDIATELY |
| After image_studio processing | Quality check output |
| Material identification | See textures, transparency, edges |
| Before background removal | Assess edge complexity |

---

## PARAMETERS

### image_path (required)

| Format | Example | Source |
|--------|---------|--------|
| Storage path | `inbox/photo.jpg` | User uploads via download_media |
| Storage path | `pending/edit.png` | image_studio output |
| URL | `https://example.com/image.jpg` | Direct URLs |

---

## WHAT YOU SEE

When you call view_image:
1. **Text metadata**: Source type, size, format
2. **Image block**: The actual image in your context

**Analyze for creative work:**
- Material (transparency, texture, finish)
- Edges (clean, fuzzy, complex)
- Background (solid, gradient, complex scene)
- Lighting (even, shadows, reflections)
- Quality (sharp, blurry, artifacts)

---

## CREATIVE PATTERNS

### Pattern 1: Pre-Processing Assessment

```python
view_image(image_path="inbox/product.jpg")
# You see: [material texture, edge complexity, background type]
# Decision: [processing approach based on what you saw]
```

### Pattern 2: Quality Check After Processing

```python
image_studio(operation="remove_bg", source="inbox/raw.jpg")
# Output: pending/processed.png

view_image(image_path="pending/processed.png")
# You see: [verify edges clean, no artifacts, transparency correct]
```

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

### Wrong: Processing Without Viewing

```
WRONG:
User: "Process inbox/item.jpg"
Agent: image_studio(remove_bg)  # Never saw the image!

CORRECT:
Agent: view_image(inbox/item.jpg)  # SEE first
# Material is glass - needs different approach
Agent: image_studio(remove_bg, preserve_transparency=true)
```

### Wrong: Repeated Viewing

```
WRONG:
view_image(inbox/item.jpg)
# ... later in same task ...
view_image(inbox/item.jpg)  # Same image!

CORRECT:
view_image(inbox/item.jpg)
# Remember what you saw, reference without re-viewing
```

---

## IMAGE SIZE NOTE

- Images auto-resized to 1024px max dimension
- Fine text may be harder to read
- Good enough for material/edge/quality assessment

</protocol>
